  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-19T00:45:56.450Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am currently making an avatar with mechanical parts, where one piece can rotate in any direction and has a sub-piece that rotates on a single axis hinge. I have placed a PhysBone on the main piece that can go in any direction and another one on the child piece set with a hinge limit.\nFor some reason, when loading the avatar, the one on the children piece has around a 50% chance of simply not working at all. It is seemingly random after each avatar reset. This behavior happens in both the Client and the SDK. Inside the SDK, copy pasting the avatar randomizes the work/not work on the copy.\nThis does not happen at all with DynamicBones. This issue does appear however with client automatic DBs to PhysBones conversion.",
